Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.710 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  in other news this morning florida's  legislature is one step closer to  passing a controversial bill that would  restrict any talk of sexual orientation  and gender identity in classrooms  critics call it the don't say gay bill  they say it would hurt lgbtq students  and families manuel bajorquez spoke with  the bill's author manny good morning  good morning that republican state  representative told us this is about a  parent's right to know what their  children are being taught and said the  subject matter is not appropriate for  the earliest grade levels but critics of  the bill call it the latest salvo in a  conservative culture war that is putting  politics ahead of vulnerable children  todd and jeff delmay say their  12-year-old son blake's public school in  hollywood florida has been a welcoming  place from preschool till  fifth grade it's been a great experience  we felt very accepted they feared the  bill that passed the florida house and a  similar one expected to pass in the  state senate could change that if  children are not feeling that they are  accepted or who they are and the family  they come from isn't accepted it will  have an impact on them the parental  rights and education bill says classroom  instruction by school personnel or third  parties on sexual orientation or gender  identity may not occur in kindergarten  through grade three parents could sue  school districts for violations  republican state representative joe  harding sponsored the house bill we want  focus to be on those basic fundamental  things the reading the writing the math  and when discussions come up as a data  for kids children ask questions  discussions are going to come up we  can't ban a conversation we can't ban a  discussion that's not what we're doing  but critics say just the threat of  lawsuits could have a chilling effect on  those discussions and language in the  bill banning those lessons when not age  appropriate or developmentally  appropriate for students in accordance  with state standards could arguably  apply to any grade joe saunders is with  equality florida so  it applies to k-12 classrooms and it  grants the right for any parent who  believes that a conversation is  happening about our families to sue a  school district it's an aggressive  attack nationwide there are 18 similar  bills moving through nine state  legislatures the advocacy group the  traver project has denounced them it  says its research shows lgbtq students  who learned about lgbtq issues or people  at school had 23 percent lower odds of  reporting a suicide attempt in the past  year you may have lgbtq youth who do not  have a supportive home environment  so  wouldn't the school be a safe place  and isn't that necessary i think the  schools are a safe place and they need  to continue to be a safe place this  wouldn't change that this doesn't change  a school being a safe place  seventeen-year-old andrew triolo says  even without the bill not all schools  are safe for people like him he is  transgender and has been bullied or  harassed he says out of every public  school he's attended i think that if i  would have had the language to express  how i felt about my gender at a younger  age it would have saved me a lot of  internal struggle and depression he  recently spoke out against the bill at  the state capitol i should get to go to  school clubs and  pick my  activities in school but i'll never get  to experience that like you did i feel  like people tend to boil down sexuality  to just sex  and that's  not what it is in the slightest i mean  there's romantic attraction there it's  culture it's it's identity it's  self-expression and that is i think very  important not to silence that  florida governor ron desantis has  signaled his support for those bills  making their way to his desk but  certainly florida is not the only  battleground the governor of texas this  week told health agencies in that state  that they should investigate gender  affirming treatments for trans  adolescents as child abuse nate  inclusivity should be something every  student has manuel thank you

